# Ajustes para clones "Pro Micro nRF52840" (compatíveis com nice!nano v2).

config ZMK_FORCE_DCDC_HV_OFF
    bool "Force nRF52840 REG0 (high-voltage) DC/DC off at boot"
    default n
    help
      Zephyr only turns the REG0 DC/DC ON when SOC_DCDC_NRF52X_HV is set; it
      never turns it off. If the bootloader left DCDCEN0 enabled, it stays on
      during ZMK. On clone boards without the REG0 inductor this can make the
      board unstable on battery. This option writes DCDCEN0 = 0 at boot.

config ZMK_FORCE_DCDC_OFF
    bool "Force nRF52840 REG1 DC/DC off at boot"
    default n
    depends on !SOC_DCDC_NRF52X
    help
      Same as above for REG1 (DCDCEN). Only allowed when the board's own DCDC
      option is disabled (CONFIG_BOARD_ENABLE_DCDC=n).
